Types of Packet Sniffing and Prevention

Passive packet sniffing involves reading data packets in transit without altering them, similar to someone reading mail without permission.
Active packet sniffing involves manipulating data packets, such as redirecting them or changing their content, akin to someone intercepting and altering mail before delivery.
To prevent malicious packet sniffing, it's recommended to use a VPN for data encryption, ensure websites use HTTPS, and avoid unprotected public Wi-Fi networks.
